Changelog: 20-11-2026 20:13:31

Added. The Voice part removes silence and saves the voice alone (owner, 20-11-2026: open a file, remove the silence
and save a copy). Remove silence cuts the silence at the start and the end of the voice. A pause inside the voice
stays. Silence below sets what counts as silence, from -60 dB to -20 dB, and the app opens with -40 dB. Each cut gets
a fade of 5 ms, so it does not click. Only the voice in the window changes, and the sound file stays as it is. Save a
copy writes the voice alone as an Ogg Vorbis, MP3, FLAC or WAV file. It never writes over the voice's own file. The
silence level is remembered with the other settings.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 16:36:28

Added. Nexus Remix Studio, a Nexus app in dev/studio/ (owner, 18-11-2026: a small remix studio, a voice track
combined with a synthesized background and saved). Nexus Dashboard has its tile. The window has three parts.

- Voice. A sound file of any rate, or a text that Text to Speech's engine speaks (From a text). The engine is Text to
  Speech's own, found in dev/text of the checkout, and nothing of it is copied.
- Background. A sustained sound made in the app. It has six presets (Warm pad, Soft strings, Drone, Glass, Choir,
  Dark), a key, an octave, a chord and the sliders Tone, Movement and Space. Try background plays 12 s of it alone.
- Mix. The volume of each track, the lead-in, the tail, the fade and, without a voice, the length. The mix is drawn
  below the sliders.

The pills at the top work on the mix. Play (Ctrl+Enter) makes the mix and plays it, Stop (Esc) ends it, and Save as
writes it as an Ogg Vorbis, MP3, FLAC or WAV file, 48 kHz stereo. Reset puts the background and the mix back on the
values the app starts with. With a voice, Length is the lead-in, the voice and the tail, and moving it changes the
tail. The mix is made in a thread, and a minute of it takes about five seconds. A mix that was
just played is saved without making it again. A mix too loud for the file is turned down as a whole, and the window
says by how much. The same settings always give the same sound.

How the background is made (remix_studio/pad.py). Each note of the chord is a few oscillators, a little out of tune
and spread left and right. An oscillator reads one cycle from a table built from harmonics, so nothing above 16 kHz is
in it. Movement fades each oscillator between a dark and a bright cycle and lets it swell. Space is a reverb, the
sound convolved in blocks with three seconds of fading noise.

A voice file is brought to 48 kHz with a windowed sinc (remix_studio/audio.py). A file is written a second at a
time to a .part file, as Text to Speech writes its speech. The app runs from the checkout with the dev venv, takes
Nexus's design and icon, and is never released (.checkout-only). install.sh writes the launcher, the menu entry and
the Desktop icon for this checkout.
